## Verdict

Revise before implementation. One MCP server and shared services are sound choices, but the plan doesn’t yet guarantee durable generation, safe concurrent editing, export fidelity or directory acceptance. The largest risks are treating credit reservations as complete idempotency and treating browser-dependent chat tools as reusable server capabilities.

## Findings

- { finding: "Queue generation lacks a durable operation protocol. A retry with a new MCP request ID can charge twice; redelivery can regenerate or overwrite newer work. A session-level generation_status cannot distinguish attempts or concurrent operations.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §3; src/db/repos/credits.ts:1239; src/db/schema.ts:373", fix: "Require an application-level idempotency key, scoped to user and operation, with an input hash. Persist operation ID, input/source revisions, reservation, result and error. Add conditional leases, fencing, terminal-result replay, an enqueue outbox, retry limits and dead-letter reconciliation. Acknowledge only after durable completion." }

- { finding: "The claim that credit safety is solid overlooks a crash window: reserveCredits deducts credits before inserting the reservation. Termination between those writes leaves a debit that the stale-reservation sweeper cannot discover.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/db/repos/credits.ts:1259,1332,1612", fix: "Atomically batch the conditional debit, ledger entry and reservation creation in D1. Couple job settlement to durable output, preserve partial refunds and prevent the 30-minute sweeper from releasing queued or actively leased work." }

- { finding: "Server persistence alone won't establish one write path. A stale dashboard still sends generated_cv, letters, emails, template and generation state wholesale, overwriting MCP changes or Queue completion. The canonical CV also contains nested structured data and screening answers that persistKit must preserve.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/hooks/useSupabaseSync.ts:78,658; src/db/repos/sessions.ts:130", fix: "Replace whole-kit sync with field-specific mutations and expected revisions. Make generation state server-owned, reject stale edits and refresh clients after conflicts. Define the complete persisted mapping, including _optimizedCVData, screening answers and document errors." }

- { finding: "The existing chat registry isn't a headless mutation layer. set_cv_template returns a client effect; CV edits return objects for the browser to apply; deletion uses confirmation chips. Mechanical edits require a prior outline call, but the catalog omits get_cv_outline.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/lib/agents/chat-tools/app-tools.ts:55; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/cv-tools.ts:104,118,206", fix: "Extract actual ownership-checked, revision-checked persistence services. Expose outline handles through get_cv or a separate tool. Replace browser chips and per-turn context with explicit MCP-compatible confirmation and revision contracts." }

- { finding: "OAuth scopes and revocation are underspecified. Defining read/write scopes doesn't establish per-tool enforcement on one mixed endpoint. Locally verified JWTs can remain usable after the Connected apps Revoke button removes a grant.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §3; [Better Auth MCP authentication](https://better-auth.com/docs/plugins/mcp)", fix: "Pass verified claims into request-local tool context and enforce scopes per operation, including resource reads. Specify grant/access-token revocation checks, refresh revocation and queued-job behavior after revocation. Test wrong audience, expired tokens, read-only writes and cross-user IDs." }

- { finding: "CIMD requires substantial Workers-specific security work absent from the spike. Better Auth's bundled transport is for Node; its documented Workers contract requires DNS resolution, special-address rejection, connection pinning and redirect refusal. Plain fetch is insufficient.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §1,§7; [Better Auth transport requirements](https://better-auth.com/docs/plugins/mcp)", fix: "Make a demonstrated compliant Workers transport an explicit go/no-go prerequisite. Cover CIMD and discovered JWKS fetches, fetch budgets and registration abuse. If unavailable, change the authorization architecture before implementing the catalog." }

- { finding: "Reading facts from D1 doesn't prevent prompt injection. An injected JD or tool result can induce the connected agent to call save_cv, delete_application or another spending tool. Existing chat protections depend on the user's current message and active application, protections MCP doesn't inherit.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §3 anti-hallucination claim; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/cv-tools.ts:35,108; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/untrusted.ts:1", fix: "Separate applicant facts from untrusted job content in outputs. Require explicit user intent for source-CV replacement and destructive actions, bind confirmation to target/revision and add hostile-JD tests that attempt CV poisoning, deletion and repeated spending." }

- { finding: "Render and download capabilities lack a security lifecycle. A short TTL doesn't prevent token leakage through request logs, analytics or referrers, and 'single-use' needs atomic redemption. A content hash isn't authorization.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §3,§4a; src/app/api/files/[...key]/route.ts:22; src/storage/paths.ts:46", fix: "Bind render capabilities to owner, operation, document and immutable revision; redeem atomically. Disable caching, analytics and referrers on print pages and redact tokens from logs. Sign an exact authorized object plus expiry, isolate cache keys by owner and define deletion/revocation behavior." }

- { finding: "Print-route authentication won't authenticate photo requests. Existing file URLs require a session cookie, which Browser Run won't have. Rendering also depends on merging structured source CV, tailored data, profile fields and photo data, not simply passing generated_cv to the template.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/app/api/files/[...key]/route.ts:22; src/components/CVPanel.tsx:181; src/lib/cv-templates/build-cv-data.ts:138", fix: "Share buildCvData with the server and resolve authorized photos directly from R2 into embedded assets. Pin the rendering input snapshot. Await fonts and image decoding before marking the page ready; fail on missing assets." }

- { finding: "'No entry is split' is impossible for an entry taller than a page. The German ATS layout uses parallel flex columns, while templates also deliberately truncate skills. Heading extraction alone won't detect lost bullets, clipping or broken reading order.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §4a; src/components/cv-templates/GermanATSTemplate.tsx:226,274; src/components/cv-templates/USPremiumATSTemplate.tsx:263", fix: "Specify print page size, margins, background printing and fragmentation rules. Keep normal entries together but allow oversized entries to split between bullets. Verify every expected visible item, reading order, blank pages and overflow, with fixtures exceeding one page per entry and spanning both columns." }

- { finding: "The cover-letter renderer can duplicate the signature. The supposedly body-only value already contains the closing and applicant name; the new layout proposes appending another signature. Structured legacy letters need a separate normalization path.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/lib/utils/cover-letter-export.ts:11; src/lib/agents/prompts/cover-letter-prompt.ts:205; PLAN.md §4a.3", fix: "Define a normalized letter model with distinct body, closing, signature and header fields. Preserve existing full-text letters without guessing delimiters, keep unknown company addresses absent and test both legacy and current formats in PDF and DOCX." }

- { finding: "A general MCP rate bucket and credit balance don't bound abuse. Parsing, screening answers, feed runs and PDF rendering consume resources without spending credits. Fresh idempotency keys also let an agent drain a balance legitimately but unintentionally.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §7; src/app/api/chat/route.ts:185; src/storage/r2.ts:37", fix: "Retain each service's entitlement and quota checks across web and MCP. Add shared per-user concurrency, daily compute/export limits and optional delegated spending budgets. Reserve capacity before enqueueing and coalesce identical exports." }

- { finding: "Several destructive annotations are wrong: regeneration and section rewriting overwrite documents, while feedback can unsave or dismiss. edit_cv_structure can remove skills from the rendered page. Reversibility doesn't justify destructiveHint:false under OpenAI's rules.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §4; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/cv-tools.ts:150; [OpenAI annotation requirements](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/plugin-guidelines)", fix: "Classify every concrete operation honestly and explicitly set all three annotations. Split feedback operations where their effects differ. Limit account output to necessary current entitlements and balance, consistent with the plan's no-plan-display mitigation." }

- { finding: "Delivery dependencies and review rows are incorrect. PR 5 can ship before exports because it depends only on PR 3. PR 4 is said to run alongside its prerequisite PR 2. Signed document access and render authorization are user-data security work, not merely a feature/design review.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §5", fix: "Make distribution depend on both catalog and exports. Parallelize only independent spikes until service contracts stabilize. Apply the Sensitive review row to export authorization and review privacy/credential handling in distribution." }

- { finding: "The preview E2E doesn't establish production Browser Run behavior. Quick Actions requires a remote binding locally, and the remote browser cannot navigate a local print URL. Queue execution also needs OpenNext's Cloudflare request context, currently entered explicitly only for scheduled work.", severity: "high", evidence: "src/worker.ts:41; src/db/client.ts:29; [Quick Actions development requirements](https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/quick-actions/)", fix: "Add queue() with equivalent context setup. Use a publicly reachable staging print route or self-contained HTML for remote rendering. Configure small consumer batches/concurrency, ID-only messages and explicit timeouts against the documented [128 KB message, 15-minute wall and default 30-second CPU limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/platform/limits/)." }

- { finding: "Distribution verification omits required submission materials and failure cases. One long successful workflow doesn't exercise every tool or directory safeguards.", severity: "high", evidence: "PLAN.md §5; [OpenAI submission requirements](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/submission); [Anthropic submission requirements](https://claude.com/docs/connectors/building/submission)", fix: "Prepare the actual versioned plugin ZIP, five positive cases, three negative cases and walkthrough video. Exercise every tool. Add retry/redelivery fault injection, stale-tab races, zero-credit accounts, revoked access and cross-user export tests. Keep reviewer credentials outside public packages and provide sufficient renewable test entitlements." }

- { finding: "Export cache invalidation is incomplete, and Browser Run concurrency pricing is misapplied.", severity: "low", evidence: "PLAN.md §4a.6, Cost; [Browser Run pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/pricing/)", fix: "Hash normalized render inputs, photo bytes, letter date, format, paper size and renderer/font version. Add retention and single-flight rendering. Quick Actions incurs browser-hours charges; concurrent-browser charges apply to Browser Sessions." }

## Missing from the plan

- **Direct editing parity:** humans can edit CV fields, cover letters and email subjects/bodies without paid regeneration. Add revision-checked editing operations. Evidence: `CVPanel.tsx:484`, `CoverLetterPanel.tsx:310`, `EmailPanel.tsx:77`.
- **Document lifecycle:** primary/master deletion and structured corrections, plus photo upload/removal. Evidence: `src/db/actions.ts:134,139`, `GeneralPane.tsx:141`.
- **Feed onboarding:** a new account cannot satisfy “consent required” through the listed tools. Specify consent, enable/disable and all editable preferences. Existing chat explicitly redirects unconfigured users to the website (`feed-tools.ts:537`).
- **Notification preferences:** tracker dates don't independently authorize reminder emails. Expose existing notification controls (`NotificationsPane.tsx:13`).
- **Async result contract:** return operation ID, pending versus actual credits, partial-document errors and polling guidance immediately. The 45-second wait should be optional, not the correctness mechanism.
- **Simplification:** extract existing repo-backed services incrementally. Prefer self-contained print HTML with embedded authorized assets if it removes print-token routes without sacrificing renderer parity.

## DISMISSED

- **One server for all clients:** appropriate; separate servers would duplicate authorization and business rules.
- **Stateless MCP and McpAgent deprecation:** confirmed by [Cloudflare's current handler documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/apis/handler-api/).
- **1.5 credits after fit:** correct in `src/lib/credit-costs.ts:3`; AGENTS.md's price table is stale.
- **Arial/Georgia availability:** both are documented [Browser Run fonts](https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/reference/supported-fonts/).
- **Client components preventing SSR:** `'use client'` alone doesn't prevent initial server rendering.
- **oklch requiring raster export:** Chromium rendering avoids html2canvas's parser limitation.
- **Existing paid accounts:** OpenAI permits access to already-purchased entitlements; checkout and upsells remain excluded.
- **Interview-prep omission:** it isn't implemented yet (`src/db/schema.ts:389`).
- **Existing repository IDOR:** sampled session/file paths check ownership; new capability URLs still require their own controls.
